{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/abyssal-exalted/885976-do-non-abyssal-exalted-regain-essence-in-the-shadowlands","id":885976,"title":"Do non-Abyssal Exalted regain Essence in the Shadowlands?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Exalted","Abyssal Exalted"],"posts":[{"date":"2016-05-08T23:13:39-07:00","id":885976,"title":"Do non-Abyssal Exalted regain Essence in the Shadowlands?","content":"Pretty much a yes/no question, but I couldn't find the answer in the main book and my Abyssal book is on loan for the foreseeable future.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1503-faradn","name":"Faradn","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1503_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"792"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-08T23:20:45-07:00","id":885980,"title":"","content":"If your main book is the Second Edition core, then the answer should be in the large sidebar at the start of... I think it's the Underworld section in the Antagonists chapter? It's on the page opposite the one with the large picture of a man driving a carriage laden with a coffin or two riding between two large beacons.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-09T13:19:58-07:00","id":886599,"title":"","content":"If 3e is consistent with previous editions, halve respiration in Shadowlands and negate it in the Underworld (Solar Exalted should be very careful in the Underworld in 3e since stunts no longer produce motes of essence).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11683-aya-tari","name":"Aya Tari","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5986"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-09T13:24:14-07:00","id":886603,"title":"","content":"Its been mentioned by devs/writers on another thread here that this will no longer be the case. Mote regen will probably be the same wherever you are. It was something like a dimension hopping thread or something. Some people seemed upset by this. And if I recall correctly the kahunas said that they hope that different dimension flavor can stand on its own without adding mechanical complications to it. Or something like that.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2746-tgueiros","name":"TGUEIROS","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2746_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1393"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-09T13:28:12-07:00","id":886606,"title":"","content":"Odd, well, I will use the previous edition rules until we get something in print myself.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11683-aya-tari","name":"Aya Tari","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5986"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-09T16:06:01-07:00","id":886707,"title":"","content":"Liminals I would imagine would respire essence the same as Abyssals do in the Underworld and Shadowlands, and any death related Exigent too.<br /> <br /> Solars/Lunars/Sidereals/Dragon Blooded respire at half in shadowlands and none in the Underworld.<br /> <br /> Fae treat both as they do creation I believe.<br /> <br /> Ghost Blooded exalts could change that, but idk.<br /> <br /> Also, this changes with Calibration for all parties.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":687,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/687-cydoc","user":"Cydoc","date":". 05-09-2016, 07:08 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/687-cydoc","name":"Cydoc","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"126"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-09T16:13:12-07:00","id":886717,"title":"","content":"This is the thread I was talking about<b></b>:<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/860352-trekking-through-other-realms-of-existence-and-your-mote-pools\">http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/m...our-mote-pools</a><br /> <br /> And here are the quotes;<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Stephen Lea Sheppard</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/860352-trekking-through-other-realms-of-existence-and-your-mote-pools?p=860547#post860547\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You'll probably just not see Ex3 refer to variable mote refresh in different realms of existence. Tracking it was shit so it's not, to my knowledge, a thing anymore.<br /> <br /> (Also it was always ridiculous because people just stunted for mote regen instead.)</div> </div> </div> </div><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Holden</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/860352-trekking-through-other-realms-of-existence-and-your-mote-pools?p=860666#post860666\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yeah it was kind of a dumb thing, because without motes you basically can't play an Exalt. Too restrictive.</div> </div> </div> </div>Of course this is subject to change, the author is dead, Golden Rule, YMMV and yada yada yada...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2746,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2746-tgueiros","user":"TGUEIROS","date":". 05-09-2016, 07:17 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2746-tgueiros","name":"TGUEIROS","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2746_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1393"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-09T16:13:28-07:00","id":886718,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aya Tari</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/abyssal-exalted/885976-do-non-abyssal-exalted-regain-essence-in-the-shadowlands?p=886606#post886606\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Odd, well, I will use the previous edition rules until we get something in print myself.</div> </div> </div> </div>You're going to have a lot of things in games abruptly change halfway through.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-09T16:16:09-07:00","id":886719,"title":"","content":"Double post.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2746-tgueiros","name":"TGUEIROS","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2746_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1393"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-09T16:19:25-07:00","id":886722,"title":"","content":"Combat is designed assuming a 5 mote per turn drip though, so cutting that might seriously break something. <br /> <br /> I mean, you're free to try it, but I'm predicting a systemic crash and burn once combat starts.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-09T16:45:18-07:00","id":886745,"title":"","content":"My understanding is that it's an unqualified &quot;yes.&quot;","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Developer for Exalted<br /> <br /> Want to write for Exalted? Look at the <a href=\"http://theonyxpath.com/submission-guidelines/\" target=\"_blank\">freelancer submission guidelines.</a><br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/user?u=451515\" target=\"_blank\">Robert Vance's Patreon</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/527-robert-vance","name":"Robert Vance","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar527_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10044"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-09T17:24:53-07:00","id":886776,"title":"","content":"Thanks guys, especially Aya.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1503-faradn","name":"Faradn","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1503_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"792"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-09T17:28:32-07:00","id":886782,"title":"","content":"Thank you, Faradn. So, are you going to run an Underworld campaign or are you just having your characters visit a Shadowland or two?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11683-aya-tari","name":"Aya Tari","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5986"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-10T08:24:23-07:00","id":887189,"title":"","content":"The net effect of the 2E regen rules was Abyssal PCs were restricted to guerrilla warfare with Creation, and every other Exalt just plain didn't want to go to the Underworld, because their players didn't want to deal with zero mote-regen, or the hassle of stunting everything.<br /> <br /> Most non-asshole STs don't try to force their players into situations they don't like, so the net result was few interesting, non-Abyssal stories revolved around the Underworld, and Abyssals didn't work well in mixed groups. <br /> <br /> Ex3's mandate includes wider roles for the Abyssals and a larger setting for everyone else, so it's not surprise this is all getting curb-kicked.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6601-totentanz","name":"Totentanz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6601_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1293"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-10T16:51:50-07:00","id":887624,"title":"","content":"Abs were capable of recovering motes of essence by draining blood, so it was not a major problem for Abs that were doing their jobs, rather than being emo Solars. The ability to recover motes of essence from killing people gave Abs incredible tactical flexibility.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11683-aya-tari","name":"Aya Tari","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5986"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-10T17:43:28-07:00","id":887681,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aya Tari</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/abyssal-exalted/885976-do-non-abyssal-exalted-regain-essence-in-the-shadowlands?p=887624#post887624\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Abs were capable of recovering motes of essence by draining blood, so it was not a major problem for Abs that were doing their jobs, rather than being emo Solars. The ability to recover motes of essence from killing people gave Abs incredible tactical flexibility.</div> </div> </div> </div>Unless you were in an area where there weren't people to munch on, or were in a situation where being seen as a cannibal monster would cause problems. So I mean sure psycho abyssal baby eater is potentially fine since they're good in a fight and they love the fighting. The diplomat who's plan was to basically get the local territories to murder the shit out of eachother, or you were playing speaker for the dead, and you're probably gonna be strained for motes if you're playing the Bishop's game of trying to convince people to join a religion based on the Underworld and Oblivion being better than the world. Just saying not really high tactical flexibility so much as just giving them a potentially bigger essence pool.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3400-nalak42","name":"nalak42","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3400_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2931"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-10T18:04:37-07:00","id":887698,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aya Tari</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/abyssal-exalted/885976-do-non-abyssal-exalted-regain-essence-in-the-shadowlands?p=887624#post887624\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Abs were capable of recovering motes of essence by draining blood, so it was not a major problem for Abs that were doing their jobs, rather than being emo Solars. The ability to recover motes of essence from killing people gave Abs incredible tactical flexibility.</div> </div> </div> </div>If you mean &quot;broke game mechanics in every combat&quot; then yes, I agree.<br /> <br /> On different note, I was able to pretty much able to run Silent Hill horror session with a group of 7 Celestials with at least 4 combat capable characters by just stopping their mote regen. This is why it's so important to change this rule - it pretty much instantly changes the tone of game if applicable.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>My homebrew/rewrites:<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/882274-new-spell-and-some-2nd-edition-spells-rewrite-for-3rd-edition-peach\" target=\"_blank\">2nd-&gt;3rd Edition Sorcery Spells Rewrite</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/823884-3e-the-artifact-and-evocation-workshop?p=890192#post890192\" target=\"_blank\">Talisman of Ten Thousand Eyes Evocations</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/913443-occult-sorcery-charms-homebrew-peach\" target=\"_blank\">Solar Occult Charms for Sorcerers</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/903155-peach-solar-thrown-charms-for-different-fighting-style-11-charms\" target=\"_blank\">Solar Thrown Charms (with Solar Danmaku Charms)</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11704-daerian","name":"Daerian","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11704_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"399"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-10T18:12:30-07:00","id":887705,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Faradn</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/abyssal-exalted/885976-do-non-abyssal-exalted-regain-essence-in-the-shadowlands#post885976\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Pretty much a yes/no question, but I couldn't find the answer in the main book and my Abyssal book is on loan for the foreseeable future.</div> </div> </div> </div> In Third Edition, you will respire Essence normally no matter where you are.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":8}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/84-holden","name":"Holden","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar84_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"673"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-10T18:14:45-07:00","id":887708,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Holden</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/abyssal-exalted/885976-do-non-abyssal-exalted-regain-essence-in-the-shadowlands?p=887705#post887705\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">In Third Edition, you will respire Essence normally no matter where you are.</div> </div> </div> </div>Holden, what about ghosts? Will they be able to respire normally in Creation, or will they be restricted to Shadowlands/Underworld? Thank you for any answer.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11683-aya-tari","name":"Aya Tari","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5986"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-10T18:20:25-07:00","id":887713,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Holden</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/abyssal-exalted/885976-do-non-abyssal-exalted-regain-essence-in-the-shadowlands?p=887705#post887705\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">In Third Edition, you will respire Essence normally no matter where you are.</div> </div> </div> </div>Oh, thank fuck, that's music to my ears!<br /> <br /> I always disliked the old 1/2 here, full there, nothing there, rules because I'd have what seemed like a cool story idea and my players would be like &quot;Yeah, sounds cool! Oh... wait... no it doesn't because we'd be screwed on essence.&quot;<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Not so noble anymore.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1823-drake","name":"Drake","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1823_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"456"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-10T18:40:27-07:00","id":887726,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Daerian</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/abyssal-exalted/885976-do-non-abyssal-exalted-regain-essence-in-the-shadowlands?p=887698#post887698\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If you mean &quot;broke game mechanics in every combat&quot; then yes, I agree.</div> </div> </div> </div>Nah - all the mote tricks in the world didn't mean a thing with the Spectral Keyword saying that you could only maintain Perfects for ten attacks, tops. 2E's mechanical flaws are a well with no bottom.<br /> <br /> On the one hand, I totally respect the rationale behind this change! Encouraging PCs of all splats to go forth and do cool stuff all over the setting is a noble goal. On the other hand, I do like occasionally putting heroes through the wringer by taking away some of their power and forcing them to find a way through anyway. Perhaps if/when it comes up in games I run, I'll reduce mote regen to 2-4 motes per hour/round.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;For me, there's no fundamental conflict between really loving something and also seeing it as very profoundly flawed.&quot; -- Jay Eddidin","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2168-chejop-kejak","name":"Chejop Kejak","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2168_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1219"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-10T20:15:14-07:00","id":887781,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nalak42</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/abyssal-exalted/885976-do-non-abyssal-exalted-regain-essence-in-the-shadowlands?p=887681#post887681\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Unless you were in an area where there weren't people to munch on, or were in a situation where being seen as a cannibal monster would cause problems. So I mean sure psycho abyssal baby eater is potentially fine since they're good in a fight and they love the fighting. The diplomat who's plan was to basically get the local territories to murder the shit out of eachother, or you were playing speaker for the dead, and you're probably gonna be strained for motes if you're playing the Bishop's game of trying to convince people to join a religion based on the Underworld and Oblivion being better than the world. Just saying not really high tactical flexibility so much as just giving them a potentially bigger essence pool.</div> </div> </div> </div>That's why you don't get caught!<br /> 1. Eat people who won't be missed.<br /> 2. Don't do it when people are watching.<br /> 3. Learn how to dispose of bodies effectively.<br /> 4. Stealth charms.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"left\"><span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">She/Her. I am literal-minded and write literally. If I don't say something explicitly, please never assume I implied it. The only exception is if I try to make a joke.</span></span></span></div> <span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">My point of view may be different from yours but is equally valid.</span></span></span><br /> <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/1x1ycoxJF0G9niMt5D3Pp7owZ7tw8AJvL?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">Exalted-cWoD-ArM url mega-library</a>. Exalted <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/663334-random-name-generator\" target=\"_blank\">name-generators</a>.","edited":{"userid":896,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/896-erinys","user":"Erinys","date":". 05-10-2016, 11:18 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/896-erinys","name":"Erinys","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar896_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4235"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-11T01:47:44-07:00","id":887989,"title":"","content":"@Aya, Actually I'm just a player, and I was curious because I don't think the ST has thought about it.<br /> <br /> I like the idea of having Lore Charms that let Celestial Exalted harvest Essence from ghosts. Abyssals harvest Essence from the denizens of Creation, Celestials harvest Essence from the denizens of the Shadowlands and Underworld. Symmetry! I don't think it's too much to ask people to take Charms just to interact with the Underworld; it would be just like how you need certain Charms to interact with the Wyld reliably.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1503-faradn","name":"Faradn","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1503_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"792"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-11T04:00:15-07:00","id":888030,"title":"","content":"I suspect ghosts will be more restricted by vulnerability to the light of day and how the Underworld is where all their stuff is.<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-11T04:08:34-07:00","id":888034,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Chejop Kejak</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/abyssal-exalted/885976-do-non-abyssal-exalted-regain-essence-in-the-shadowlands?p=887726#post887726\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">On the one hand, I totally respect the rationale behind this change! Encouraging PCs of all splats to go forth and do cool stuff all over the setting is a noble goal. On the other hand, I do like occasionally putting heroes through the wringer by taking away some of their power and forcing them to find a way through anyway. Perhaps if/when it comes up in games I run, I'll reduce mote regen to 2-4 motes per hour/round.</div> </div> </div> </div>Alternatively if you wanted to run a session or two with reduced/no mote recovery this seems like it could be the effect of an abyssal manse, or underworld artifact or Necromanic working. Basically if you want to run a story where this is the case there are ways to do it, but you aren't shoehorned into doing it all the time. I gotta say I find the change very welcome.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9124-satoshi","name":"satoshi","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"282"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-11T04:12:08-07:00","id":888037,"title":"","content":"I mean, if you think about it, the whole Abyssal vampire thing never made a great deal of sense. <br /> <br /> You can't respire life essence, so instead you suck it out of people... who by all rights should be running off the very sort of essence you can't process. Yeah, someone didn't entirely think this through.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-11T04:21:29-07:00","id":888041,"title":"","content":"I think the method constitutes a bit of a transitional thing.<br /> <br /> I think that's a bit like saying &quot;ghosts can't be associated with deathly Essence, or even exist at all, because they were alive when they died&quot;.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-11T07:50:45-07:00","id":888195,"title":"","content":"Yeah, I think stealling it from the living by the medium of blood, especially while killing them, transforms it into deathly Essence that's easy to respire.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"left\"><span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">She/Her. I am literal-minded and write literally. If I don't say something explicitly, please never assume I implied it. The only exception is if I try to make a joke.</span></span></span></div> <span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">My point of view may be different from yours but is equally valid.</span></span></span><br /> <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/1x1ycoxJF0G9niMt5D3Pp7owZ7tw8AJvL?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">Exalted-cWoD-ArM url mega-library</a>. Exalted <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/663334-random-name-generator\" target=\"_blank\">name-generators</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/896-erinys","name":"Erinys","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar896_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4235"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-11T12:25:32-07:00","id":888436,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Chejop Kejak</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/abyssal-exalted/885976-do-non-abyssal-exalted-regain-essence-in-the-shadowlands?p=887726#post887726\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Nah - all the mote tricks in the world didn't mean a thing with the Spectral Keyword saying that you could only maintain Perfects for ten attacks, tops. 2E's mechanical flaws are a well with no bottom.</div> </div> </div> </div>Why? You regenerated more motes than other Exalted per turn by wounding/killing and used stunts for Willpower instead. It was broken (no Ink Monkeys/ Dawn solution/ 2.5 errata ofc).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>My homebrew/rewrites:<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/882274-new-spell-and-some-2nd-edition-spells-rewrite-for-3rd-edition-peach\" target=\"_blank\">2nd-&gt;3rd Edition Sorcery Spells Rewrite</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/823884-3e-the-artifact-and-evocation-workshop?p=890192#post890192\" target=\"_blank\">Talisman of Ten Thousand Eyes Evocations</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/913443-occult-sorcery-charms-homebrew-peach\" target=\"_blank\">Solar Occult Charms for Sorcerers</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/903155-peach-solar-thrown-charms-for-different-fighting-style-11-charms\" target=\"_blank\">Solar Thrown Charms (with Solar Danmaku Charms)</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11704-daerian","name":"Daerian","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11704_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"399"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-11T13:05:49-07:00","id":888485,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Daerian</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/abyssal-exalted/885976-do-non-abyssal-exalted-regain-essence-in-the-shadowlands?p=888436#post888436\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Why? You regenerated more motes than other Exalted per turn by wounding/killing and used stunts for Willpower instead. It was broken (no Ink Monkeys/ Dawn solution/ 2.5 errata ofc).</div> </div> </div> </div>My experience with 2e Celestial combat is that very little wounding/killing happened until the fight was effectively resolved. Everyone fired their Paranoia Combos (Xm, 1wp) all the time, and stunted twice (one attack, one defense) - one for 1 wp, the other for 4m. Abyssals, though, had to spend 2wp for the combo. In theory, they could gain more than 4m by wounding people, but in practice, Perfect Defenses. So, they ran out of motes fastest, then died.<br /> <br /> Unless, of course, they were in a Shadowland/the Underworld, which brings us to the point of this thread: that despite the cool flavor of having difficulties operating on the &quot;wrong&quot; Realm, in practice, it tended to be a massive nerf... which is presumably why it's not sticking around.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;For me, there's no fundamental conflict between really loving something and also seeing it as very profoundly flawed.&quot; -- Jay Eddidin","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2168-chejop-kejak","name":"Chejop Kejak","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2168_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1219"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-11T13:09:50-07:00","id":888490,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Chejop Kejak</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/abyssal-exalted/885976-do-non-abyssal-exalted-regain-essence-in-the-shadowlands?p=888485#post888485\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">My experience with 2e Celestial combat is that very little wounding/killing happened until the fight was effectively resolved.</div> </div> </div> </div>That's for what extras are ;-)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>My homebrew/rewrites:<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/882274-new-spell-and-some-2nd-edition-spells-rewrite-for-3rd-edition-peach\" target=\"_blank\">2nd-&gt;3rd Edition Sorcery Spells Rewrite</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/823884-3e-the-artifact-and-evocation-workshop?p=890192#post890192\" target=\"_blank\">Talisman of Ten Thousand Eyes Evocations</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/913443-occult-sorcery-charms-homebrew-peach\" target=\"_blank\">Solar Occult Charms for Sorcerers</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/903155-peach-solar-thrown-charms-for-different-fighting-style-11-charms\" target=\"_blank\">Solar Thrown Charms (with Solar Danmaku Charms)</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11704-daerian","name":"Daerian","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11704_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"399"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-11T18:06:05-07:00","id":888713,"title":"","content":"Never used extras in my games. Even the giant rats were given fair treatment.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11683-aya-tari","name":"Aya Tari","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5986"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-11T19:59:53-07:00","id":888788,"title":"","content":"One thing to consider;<br /> <br /> Why the hell does someone design something that sucks while trying to achieve its purpose?<br /> <br /> Abyssals were supposed to be invaders intent on bringing down Creation, they were developed by their masters for that. So why do they suck at being in Creation, when that is needed to fulfill their purposes? They did not evolve through millions of years in one environment and then were tossed into another were they should suffer. They were made to be in that environment, an environment where they suck at being at. Who does that?<br /> <br /> Its like an engineer designing a desert crossing vehicle that sports the &quot;quirk&quot; of sucking while crossing sand. It is a fairly dull proposition and I'm glad it is gone.<br /> <br /> I can see some weakening or enfeeblement be thematic, but cutting respiration is just too castrating.<br /> <br /> P.S. The same can be said of Solars, Infernals and whatever. They were made by the Mightiest Forces of the Universe<span style=\"font-family:AppleSDGothicNeo-Regular, lucida grande, tahoma, verdana, arial, sans-serif, Segoe UI Emoji, Segoe UI Symbol, NotoColorEmoji, EmojiSymbols, Symbola, Noto, Android Emoji, AndroidEmoji, Arial Unicode MS, Zapf Dingbats, AppleColorEmoji, Apple Color Emoji\"><span style=\"color:#000000\">\u2122 to be all around heroes, go to incredibly hostile places and win. They shouldn't shrink when they leave their homes.</span></span>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2746-tgueiros","name":"TGUEIROS","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2746_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1393"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-11T20:06:07-07:00","id":888790,"title":"","content":"I think the idea was that the Neverborn weren't able to make Abyssals any better with living essence than that. The Neverborn are dead, the Deathlords are dead, and Abyssals are modified to be more-or-less undead. And in 1E-2E, if Abyssals didn't have that limitation, the Deathlords would have conquered Creation without facing any real opposition, so... it made sense at the time, and made Creation slightly less Doomed.<br /> <br /> Whether or not it was a bad game mechanic is a separate question.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"left\"><span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">She/Her. I am literal-minded and write literally. If I don't say something explicitly, please never assume I implied it. The only exception is if I try to make a joke.</span></span></span></div> <span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">My point of view may be different from yours but is equally valid.</span></span></span><br /> <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/1x1ycoxJF0G9niMt5D3Pp7owZ7tw8AJvL?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">Exalted-cWoD-ArM url mega-library</a>. Exalted <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/663334-random-name-generator\" target=\"_blank\">name-generators</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/896-erinys","name":"Erinys","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar896_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4235"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-11T20:33:30-07:00","id":888803,"title":"","content":"I think it allowed the Abs to be appropriate bad guys.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11683-aya-tari","name":"Aya Tari","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5986"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-12T10:05:23-07:00","id":889214,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aya Tari</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/abyssal-exalted/885976-do-non-abyssal-exalted-regain-essence-in-the-shadowlands?p=888713#post888713\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Never used extras in my games. Even the giant rats were given fair treatment.</div> </div> </div> </div>In the sort of combat environment 2E created, anything that couldn't perfect <i>was</i> an extra.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><hr /><i>The difference between fiction and reality? Fiction has to make sense.</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/434-astralporing","name":"Astralporing","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar434_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"296"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-12T10:15:07-07:00","id":889219,"title":"","content":"I dunno, my infernal once got into a fight where he couldn't use his perfect (it was the Malfean one and he was in the middle of a field) and managed to win after taking enough damage to kill a normal human about 6 times over.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-12T11:00:41-07:00","id":889243,"title":"","content":"This thread is probably not the place to rehash old debates about 2E combat mechanics. I, at least, shall never use them again.<br /> <br /> One thing it does have me thinking about is other possible ways to make different realms of existence mechanically odd. Taking away mote regen is too harsh, sure, but I still feel like the Underworld should be more than &quot;a creepy ocean with spooky monsters.&quot; Ditto Yu-Shan as &quot;a pretty city full of Essence-Users,&quot; and Malfeas as &quot;an ugly city full of creepy Essence-users&quot;. What tricks might work? The first thing to come to my mind is giving out a blanket penalty to Awareness rolls in the Underworld, which would both make it harder to notice scary things coming towards you (for that slight shift towards the horror genre) and be a meaningful combat debuff (Join Battle, and all).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;For me, there's no fundamental conflict between really loving something and also seeing it as very profoundly flawed.&quot; -- Jay Eddidin","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2168-chejop-kejak","name":"Chejop Kejak","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2168_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1219"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-12T11:02:28-07:00","id":889244,"title":"","content":"Playing up Malfeas' completely wonky geography might be an option.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-12T11:05:33-07:00","id":889246,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Elfive</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/abyssal-exalted/885976-do-non-abyssal-exalted-regain-essence-in-the-shadowlands?p=889244#post889244\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Playing up Malfeas' completely wonky geography might be an option.</div> </div> </div> </div>Cool concept! How would you go about that?<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;For me, there's no fundamental conflict between really loving something and also seeing it as very profoundly flawed.&quot; -- Jay Eddidin","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2168-chejop-kejak","name":"Chejop Kejak","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2168_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1219"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-12T11:36:10-07:00","id":889264,"title":"","content":"Another thing that could occur is strange healing and healing Charm effects. Healing in the Underworld should be less effective, there is no life essence, while healing in Malfeas and the Wyld should be twisted. I would rule in my games that normal mortals are capable of taking a total of seven health levels of damage, regardless of healing, before becoming ghosts in the Underworld, first circle demons in Malfeas, common fair folk in the Wyld, etc. Each week that a normal mortal spends back in Creation would reduce the accumulated total by one, until it reset to '0'. That would make other realms even more terrifying for normal mortals.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11683-aya-tari","name":"Aya Tari","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5986"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-12T12:01:44-07:00","id":889281,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Erinys</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/abyssal-exalted/885976-do-non-abyssal-exalted-regain-essence-in-the-shadowlands?p=888790#post888790\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> And in 1E-2E, if Abyssals didn't have that limitation, the Deathlords would have conquered Creation without facing any real opposition, so... it made sense at the time, and made Creation slightly less Doomed.</div> </div> </div> </div>I disagree that this was the case.<br /> We're only talking five years, in which time the majority of Solar Exalted whose Exaltations were trapped in the Jade Prison haven't done much besides foster their power in secret. The Abyssals aren't that much better organised, the Deathlords might give them resources to complete their tasks but we've also got instances of Abyssals who haven't been allowed to be competent in their natural field because of their master's quirks it's also not hard to believe there's a lot of infighting.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><a href=\"https://swordofcreation.net/\" target=\"_blank\">Sword of Creation</a> a hub for Exalted related content</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7-lioness","name":"Lioness","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7_2.png","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5443"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-12T20:30:23-07:00","id":889593,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Erinys</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/abyssal-exalted/885976-do-non-abyssal-exalted-regain-essence-in-the-shadowlands?p=888790#post888790\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think the idea was that the Neverborn weren't able to make Abyssals any better with living essence than that. The Neverborn are dead, the Deathlords are dead, and Abyssals are modified to be more-or-less undead. And in 1E-2E, if Abyssals didn't have that limitation, the Deathlords would have conquered Creation without facing any real opposition, so... it made sense at the time, and made Creation slightly less Doomed.<br /> <br /> Whether or not it was a bad game mechanic is a separate question.</div> </div> </div> </div>No real opposition? 100 Sids, Thousands of DBs, Hundreds of Lunars, Thousands of Gods, Godblooded, Heroic Mortals etc.. And the other 150 Solars? Is there something I am missing here?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2746-tgueiros","name":"TGUEIROS","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2746_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1393"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-12T21:51:43-07:00","id":889645,"title":"","content":"I was attempting to be slightly flippant about how overpowered the Deathlords were and how inevitable their takeover was made to appear. Obviously I phrased it badly! I can't word sometimes.<br /> <br /> Could conquer Creation... even more easily? Even faster? I'm still at a loss for words but it wasn't important or anything.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"left\"><span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">She/Her. I am literal-minded and write literally. If I don't say something explicitly, please never assume I implied it. The only exception is if I try to make a joke.</span></span></span></div> <span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">My point of view may be different from yours but is equally valid.</span></span></span><br /> <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/1x1ycoxJF0G9niMt5D3Pp7owZ7tw8AJvL?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">Exalted-cWoD-ArM url mega-library</a>. Exalted <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/663334-random-name-generator\" target=\"_blank\">name-generators</a>.","edited":{"userid":896,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/896-erinys","user":"Erinys","date":". 05-13-2016, 12:55 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/896-erinys","name":"Erinys","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar896_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4235"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-13T19:20:28-07:00","id":890339,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TGUEIROS</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/abyssal-exalted/885976-do-non-abyssal-exalted-regain-essence-in-the-shadowlands?p=888788#post888788\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">One thing to consider;<br /> <br /> Why the hell does someone design something that sucks while trying to achieve its purpose?<br /> <br /> Abyssals were supposed to be invaders intent on bringing down Creation, they were developed by their masters for that. So why do they suck at being in Creation, when that is needed to fulfill their purposes? They did not evolve through millions of years in one environment and then were tossed into another were they should suffer. They were made to be in that environment, an environment where they suck at being at. Who does that?<br /> <br /> Its like an engineer designing a desert crossing vehicle that sports the &quot;quirk&quot; of sucking while crossing sand. It is a fairly dull proposition and I'm glad it is gone.<br /> <br /> I can see some weakening or enfeeblement be thematic, but cutting respiration is just too castrating.<br /> <br /> P.S. The same can be said of Solars, Infernals and whatever. They were made by the Mightiest Forces of the Universe<span style=\"font-family:AppleSDGothicNeo-Regular, lucida grande, tahoma, verdana, arial, sans-serif, Segoe UI Emoji, Segoe UI Symbol, NotoColorEmoji, EmojiSymbols, Symbola, Noto, Android Emoji, AndroidEmoji, Arial Unicode MS, Zapf Dingbats, AppleColorEmoji, Apple Color Emoji\"><span style=\"color:#000000\">\u2122 to be all around heroes, go to incredibly hostile places and win. They shouldn't shrink when they leave their homes.</span></span></div> </div> </div> </div>Exalted, as I understand it, aren't really <i>designed</i>. They're based on the flavor of whatever empowers them. I would assume that the need that requires their creation has some influence on which aspects of their patron are emphasized (so eg. a harvest god who empowers an Exigent for combat will probably get one which emphasizes the parts of their themes appropriate to combat), but they can't just say &quot;I want it to work like this, not like that&quot;; some of the patron's weaknesses and limitations are going to be there no matter what. No matter how much they may want to, the Unconquered Sun can't create Lunars, and Luna can't create Solars; the harvest god's exigent is always going to have a lot of charms that help with harvests.<br /> <br /> (Of course, realm-specific mote regeneration is still a bad idea for the gameplay reasons people have already have mentioned.)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":517,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/517-aquillion","user":"Aquillion","date":". 05-13-2016, 10:22 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/517-aquillion","name":"Aquillion","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar517_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1341"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-17T18:14:56-07:00","id":892902,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aquillion</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/abyssal-exalted/885976-do-non-abyssal-exalted-regain-essence-in-the-shadowlands?p=890339#post890339\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Exalted, as I understand it, aren't really <i>designed</i>. They're based on the flavor of whatever empowers them. I would assume that the need that requires their creation has some influence on which aspects of their patron are emphasized (so eg. a harvest god who empowers an Exigent for combat will probably get one which emphasizes the parts of their themes appropriate to combat), but they can't just say &quot;I want it to work like this, not like that&quot;; some of the patron's weaknesses and limitations are going to be there no matter what. No matter how much they may want to, the Unconquered Sun can't create Lunars, and Luna can't create Solars; the harvest god's exigent is always going to have a lot of charms that help with harvests.<br /> <br /> (Of course, realm-specific mote regeneration is still a bad idea for the gameplay reasons people have already have mentioned.)</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I believe you may have read more into &quot;design&quot; than what I tried to convey with the use of the word. You are suggesting a level of control and attention to aesthetics and minutiae that is not what I am arguing.<br /> <br /> What I mean is that the Exaltations were made with a purpose and therefore should be suited to fulfill that purpose. They are not a spontaneous expression of Divinity that just happened.<br /> <br /> Solars were created to lay low the God's Gods and then be the Masters of Creation. Abyssals are intentionally and specifically modified to hand Creation to their Master's desires. In my opinion they shouldn't be crippled by stepping outside their homes, that fact would just make the whole thing jarring and incongruous with what I believe Exaltation represents.<br /> <br /> Its like saying Achilles should have lost his invulnerability when he left Greece and should have been just a great soldier while in Troy.<br /> <br /> I don't see Exalts as the regular boy answering a Great Calling who comes undone on the Swamp of Sadness and needs to be saved by someone else. They might fall to its dangers, but they will have blazed a trail and left their mark on it.<br /> <br /> Again this is just my opinion. I'm not against some side effects, as long as they are a nuisance not some crippling condition. Also, I am completely for some specific parts of the world being incredibly hazardous, but that goes for anywhere, be it Creation, the Underworld, Malfeas, Yu-Shan, the Wyld or wherever else.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2746-tgueiros","name":"TGUEIROS","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2746_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1393"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-18T04:43:15-07:00","id":893205,"title":"","content":"It's funny, because Achilleus didn't <i>have</i> invulnerability in a good portion of his legend - in fact, it seems to be one of those later additions to the story. If he was invulnerable, why would he worry about his armor having been taken after dearest Patroclus was slain?<br /> <br /> It's sorta like when a sequel song was written for &quot;Big Bad John&quot; - he went from a self-sacrificing hero to a tall tale who goes on to have a hundred and ten grandchildren with his &quot;Cajun Queen.&quot;","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>He/him","edited":{"userid":177,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","user":"TheCountAlucard","date":". 05-18-2016, 07:55 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","name":"TheCountAlucard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar177_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10857"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-19T10:47:32-07:00","id":894165,"title":"","content":"@TheCountAlucard<br /> <br /> I never read any Achilles story where his invulnerabilty (sans heel) wasn't part of the story.<br /> <br /> Where is that from? Is it from some study on the origin of the story or a personal musing? (Genuinely curious btw, not snide)<br /> <br /> Being that Patroclus used his armor to impersonate him maybe he just wanted it back as a treasured possession a loved one died with and its strong association with him. <br /> <br /> Back then having an unique armor was probably a calling card. Few people would know a face, but many could have heard about a specific armor design. Maybe he wanted ut back because of that too.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2746-tgueiros","name":"TGUEIROS","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2746_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1393"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-19T20:09:26-07:00","id":894522,"title":"","content":"Or maybe he wanted it back because he sank so much XP into its evocations.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/456-blackwell","name":"Blackwell","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar456_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"977"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-19T21:27:51-07:00","id":894552,"title":"","content":"If I recall there's a lengthy bit in the Illiad about Achille's shield and how amazing it was and I think it was made by Hephaestus. So if it was gift ,particularly from his mother or a god, it would be kind of really important. Plus I believe he wanted the armor because his best friend was in the armor and he had kind of sworn to bring him back home. (Having already royally fucked up the making sure said friend survives by his little limit break earlier in the epic.)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3400-nalak42","name":"nalak42","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3400_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2931"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-20T05:15:43-07:00","id":894664,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TGUEIROS</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/abyssal-exalted/885976-do-non-abyssal-exalted-regain-essence-in-the-shadowlands?p=894165#post894165\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I never read any Achilles story where his invulnerabilty (sans heel) wasn't part of the story.<br /> <br /> Where is that from?</div> </div> </div> </div>Right in the <i>Iliad</i>. His invulnerability never even gets a mention, and moreover, he gets injured pretty noticeably (and <b>not on the heel!</b>) near the end - he even bleeds.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TGUEIROS</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/abyssal-exalted/885976-do-non-abyssal-exalted-regain-essence-in-the-shadowlands?p=894165#post894165\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Being that Patroclus used his armor to impersonate him maybe he just wanted it back as a treasured possession a loved one died with and its strong association with him.</div> </div> </div> </div>No, I'm talking about the part where he's saying (paraphrased): &quot;Damn! I can't go out there to avenge Patroclus because Patroclus went out there <i>in my armor</i>, and now it's in the enemy's hands.&quot; He doesn't even monologue about going out there <i>without</i> any armor, because he knows (and presumably the audience knows) that if he does, he's gonna get fucking killed.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nalak42</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/abyssal-exalted/885976-do-non-abyssal-exalted-regain-essence-in-the-shadowlands?p=894552#post894552\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If I recall there's a lengthy bit in the Illiad about Achille's shield and how amazing it was and I think it was made by Hephaestus.</div> </div> </div> </div>That's given to him <i>afterward</i>, as part of a magnificent set of armor, specifically given to him so he is able to go out there and avenge Patroclus.<br /> <br /> _____________<br /> Okay, guys, let me get real with you for a second. <br /> <br /> No, there's no <i>explicit</i> part of the <i>Iliad</i> in which Achilles or his mother or Zeus or anybody else turns to the camera and says, &quot;For this story, Achilles isn't invulnerable, guys,&quot; because at the time of the <i>Iliad</i>'s writing, it wasn't even part of the Achilles myth. <br /> <br /> The <i>Iliad</i> is the Greek equivalent of <i>Action Comics no. 1</i>. It tells one of the most familiar stories in all of Greek myth, but like <i>Action Comics no. 1</i>, a huge number of people haven't actually read it*, and the main character doesn't have the superpowers that later got piled onto him (or for Supes, <b>the shit-ton</b> of superpowers).<br /> <br /> *Going through a tiny excerpt as part of your high school English class doesn't count, dammit.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>He/him","edited":{"userid":177,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","user":"TheCountAlucard","date":". 05-20-2016, 08:58 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","name":"TheCountAlucard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar177_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10857"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}